  "tags": ["csharp", "recursion", "math", "easy"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Problem Statement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Given a base `n` and exponent `p`, compute `n^p`."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Input:** `n = 9`, `p = 9`\n\n**Output:** `387420489`"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Approach 1: Linear Recursion"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Multiply `n` by itself `p` times recursively. O(p) time, O(p) stack."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Linear Recursion O(p)",
        "content": "Multiply n by itself p times recursively.",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "public long PowerLinear(int n, int p)\n{\n    if (p == 0) return 1;\n    return n * PowerLinear(n, p - 1);\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Approach 2: Binary Exponentiation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use exponentiation by squaring: if `p` is even, `n^p = (n^(p/2))²`; if odd, `n^p = n * (n^(p/2))²`. O(log p) time."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Binary Exponentiation O(log p)",
        "content": "Use exponentiation by squaring to reduce the number of multiplications.",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "public long PowerBinary(int n, int p)\n{\n    if (p == 0) return 1;\n    long half = PowerBinary(n, p / 2);\n    if (p % 2 == 0)\n        return half * half;\n    return n * half * half;\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "tip",
        "title": "What improved?",
        "text": "**Time:** O(p) → O(log p). **Space:** O(p) → O(log p). Binary exponentiation halves the exponent at each step, making it exponentially faster."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "comparison-cards",
      "data": {
